  "thought": "The layer rank views reveal several important patterns. The top latency layers are all layer0_ffn1_tiling0-7 with identical 8.27s latency each, and they dominate the compute dimension (99.98% compute share). The critical-end view shows layer0_norm2 (19.70s) and layer0_res2 (19.70s) as the latest-finishing layers, followed by ffn2 tilings. The aggregate breakdown shows 67.6% compute time, 17.8% memory, 14.6% communication. For energy, memory dominates at 49.8%, communication at 26.7%, compute at 22.4%. I should now look at operator groups to understand the overall layer composition and then check the execution timeline for idle gaps and core utilization.",
  "action": "tool",
  "tool": {
    "name": "summarize_operator_groups",
    "arguments": {
      "sort_by": "latency_sum",
      "top_groups": 8,
      "include_components": true
    }
  }
}

